#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS Access model"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Role decides reach, entitlements decide rows, classification decides columns."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: governance · depends on: [CAP-IDENTITY]{1}, [CAP-CATALOG]{2}, [CAP-CLASSIFICATION]{3}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Decide access from three independent inputs: role, scope and sensitivity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "No single change can widen access across all three ([P14]{1}). Exemptions are named because each is a path to raw data ([P5]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Groups for reach; an entitlement table for rows; classification tags for columns."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "One row-filter function per class of table; masks per classification."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Anyone exempt from a policy, any holder of a manage right, and the catalog administrator effectively see raw data. Keep those lists short and reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Reach (which catalogs and actions) is granted to identity-provider groups by role."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Every grant's principal is a group mapped to a role."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Row scope comes from an entitlement table derived from an authoritative feed (for example staff postings), with a validity period, never edited by hand.{1}*Example:* An officer posted to District B sees District B's learners; when the posting ends on 31 August, the rows disappear from their queries that day, with no one editing a permission."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "The entitlement table is written only by its loader; a manual write is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Row and column policies only narrow access. Each user and table resolves to exactly one row filter and each column to at most one mask; an ambiguity fails the query rather than choosing.{1}*Example:* A user who is a teacher at one school and an officer for a district would match two row filters on the learner table; the query fails until one scope is chosen, rather than silently using the wider one."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Test a user matching two filters; the query fails."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Only pipeline identities are exempt from policies, each exemption listed with its reason."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "The exemption list contains only workload identities, each with a reason."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Access to identifiable columns is through a time-boxed, audited group."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Membership of the group expires; each grant appears in audit."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Reach, row scope and classification are each changed by a different owner, so no single change widens access across all three.{1}*Example:* Joining the analyst group gives a person reach but no rows until the posting feed gives them a scope, and no special-category columns unless a steward's classification allows them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "The owners of the group declarations, the entitlement feed and the classification rules are different roles."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Row scope may also come from a relationship (the record is the person's own, or the person is a guardian with verified authority), taken from the authoritative relationship record, effective-dated, and ended when the relationship or the authority ends.{1}*Example:* A guardian sees their child's attendance; when a court order ends their authority on 1 March, the next query after that date returns nothing."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Ending a guardian relationship removes access at the next query."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "CAP-ACCESS.8"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "A view for a data subject or guardian exposes a declared, minimal set of columns per record class; designated special-category fields are excluded from guardian views by default, with the reason recorded.{1}*Example:* The guardian view of a learner shows enrolment, attendance and results, but not counselling notes, which are excluded by default with the reason recorded."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-access.md
msgid "Subject-facing views are declared in code with their column lists and exclusions."
msgstr ""

